course: dictionary
lesson: 12894
title: Epistle: a long, formal letter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An epistle is an old word for a letter, usually a long and formal one. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it for clues. «The vicar read an epistle from the New Testament during the service.» The words read and service tell you that an epistle is a written letter that is read aloud.
explain: In the Bible, the Epistles are letters written by early Christian leaders such as Paul, Peter and John, sent to churches or to people. «The Epistle to the Romans» is one of them. Their titles often begin with «The Epistle to…» or «The First Epistle of…».
explain: People sometimes use the word as a joke. «Grandma's epistle about the garden ran to eight pages.» Calling a short note an epistle makes it sound grand and serious, so the reader knows the letter is very long. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: An epistle is a letter, usually a long and formal one.
fact: In the Bible, the Epistles are letters from early Christian leaders such as Paul, Peter and John.
fact: «The Epistle reading» is the part of a church service where one of these letters is read aloud.
fact: «The Epistle to the Romans» and «The First Epistle of John» are books in the New Testament.
fact: Calling a letter «an epistle» as a joke means it is very long or serious.
exercise: «The vicar read an epistle during the service.» What is an epistle here? | *A letter | A prayer book | A church bell | A kind of hymn
exercise: Which of these is a book of the New Testament that is an Epistle? | Exodus | Genesis | Psalms | *The Epistle to the Romans
exercise: «Grandma's epistle about the garden ran to eight pages.» What does the joke suggest? | A short note on a sticky label | *A very long, serious letter | A map of the garden | A song about gardens
test: In church, «the Epistle reading» means what? | *A reading from one of the letters in the New Testament | A list of hymn numbers | A prayer said in silence | A song the choir sings
test: In everyday talk, what does «an epistle» usually mean? | A quick text message | *A long, formal letter | A piece of music | A type of sandwich
exam: «The First Epistle of John» is found in which part of the Bible? | In a school library only | In the Old Testament | In a shop catalogue | *In the New Testament
